From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 13 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: share the fold helpers of the Lua libraries, fix FFA
 absolute range and Destroy of a gone token at n > 2

Move the local fold helpers of libduel, libcard and libgroup into fold_lib.h
(namespace fold, inline, one name per job). This step is a pure move and rename.
Group.SelectWithSumEqual and SelectWithSumGreater clear the stale forced
cards at n > 2 when the chooser is not a living seat.
field::add_effect swaps the two ranges of an absolute FFA effect when the new
owner is another duelist, so the named side stays the named side.
Destroy drops a card that has no location and no controller. A script can keep
a group with a token that already left the field. Such a token has controler
0xFF at n > 2 and it was indexed into hint_timing. Destroy and Equip also write
no hint timing for a card without a controller. The n == 2 path is unchanged.
Param kinds PLAYER_EITHER and 0x10 in operation info are not folded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
